# Canonical host redirects (Apache / OVH mutualisé).
# Consolidate every URL variant to https://gpoussel.fr so Google sees a single
# canonical host. Without this, http://, www. and http://www. variants surface in
# Search Console as "Alternate page with proper canonical tag" duplicates.
# Files in public/ are copied verbatim to dist/ and deployed to the web root.

# Disable Apache directory auto-indexing. There is no src/pages/blog/index.astro,
# so without this the host falls back to its raw "Index of /blog" listing for
# /blog/ (HTTP 200, indexable, leaking the post slug folders). Defense-in-depth
# so no other folder can ever leak a listing either.
Options -Indexes

RewriteEngine On

# www -> non-www and http -> https, all to https://gpoussel.fr (single 301).
# If OVH terminates SSL upstream and this causes a redirect loop, swap the
# second condition for: RewriteCond %{HTTP:X-Forwarded-Proto} !https
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} ^www\. [NC,OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTPS} !=on
RewriteRule ^ https://gpoussel.fr%{REQUEST_URI} [R=301,L]

# /blog/ (and /blog) has no index page: the home route (/) is already the full
# paginated writing list that NAV's "Writing" points at. Redirect to it (301) so
# the bare collection root is a real, on-brand, canonical landing instead of the
# directory listing. Anchored to the exact path so /blog/<slug>/ posts are
# untouched.
RewriteRule ^blog/?$ https://gpoussel.fr/ [R=301,L]
